  "notes": "Four detectors, one from each side, so every voxel is seen from more than one direction. The void is a 3 m capsule buried at the mid-plane: unlike the default scene's corridor it does not break either surface, so a single view cannot separate it from a density variation along the ray, and a smoothness prior will flatten it. This is the scene A4's one-sided anchor and the ordered-subset acceleration criterion are tested on; the default scene stays as it is so its golden counts and the A1 measurements on them remain valid."
